> DMS Settings - System and Plugins

In-depth guide to DMS system settings and plugin management (super+S > system, plugins).

### Audio

output device: select default speaker/headphones.
input device: select default microphone.
volume levels: set default volumes.
audio profiles: switch between audio configurations.

### Clipboard Manager

clipboard history size: number of entries to keep.
clipboard persistence: keep clipboard contents after application closes.
image clipboard: enable/disable image clipboard support.
invoked with *super+V* or bar widget.

### Multiplexer/Tiling

mangoWM tiling settings accessible from DMS:
layout switching behavior.
window gap preferences (syncs with decoration.conf).
focus follows mouse behavior.

### Network

wifi: scan and connect to networks.
ethernet: manage wired connections.
VPN: add and manage VPN connections.
connection priority: order of preferred networks.

### Bluetooth

bluetooth on/off toggle.
pair new devices.
manage paired devices.
file transfer over bluetooth.

### Displays

graphical display configuration:
monitor layout (position, arrangement).
resolution and refresh rate per monitor.
fractional scaling per monitor.
mirror/extend display modes.

### Power/Sleep

screen blank timeout.
suspend/idle timeout.
power button behavior.
sleep inhibit toggle (bound to *super+I*).

### Lock Screen

lock screen style and timeout.
lock on sleep/wake.
manual lock with *super+L*.
screen saver settings.

### Plugin Management

DMS supports plugins to extend functionality.

available plugins include:
FlatpakUpdates: automatic flatpak update notifications.

to install plugins:
1. go to settings > plugins.
2. browse available plugins.
3. click install on desired plugins.
4. enabled plugins activate automatically.

custom plugins can be added to ~/.config/dms/plugins/
